:1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T20:24:09-07:00","id":721595,"title":"","content":"Thanks!<br /> <br /> My understanding is that Kumo don't follow Ananasa in any way. She gave them to the Wyrm... but they don't serve her. The Damhan (werespiders loyal to Queen Ananasa) who are marked to emulate the Balance Wyrm are named Hatar. I'm going by Breedbook Ananasi, PGttCB, and Hengeyokai, so Revised and 2E. Did W20 retcon the Kumo?<br /> <br /> I would imagine Antara to be the Damhan who fall to the Wyrm without joining the Kumo organization or revering their three spirits (Rati, Marawa, Nareau).<br /> <br /> Oh apparently I wrote down the name Breakers as a group of Wyrm Ananasi. Don't remember where I got that or anything about them. Maybe they're the same as Antara.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you know of any way to access the Ozuzo article? I can't find it at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Out of all these fallen jerks, which ones are organized groups that have their own kinfolk and society, and which are (or were) just individual jerks? Off the top of my head when I should be going to bed:<br /> <br /> Ajaba -- Ozuzo (?)<br /> Ananasi -- Antara (?)<br /> Ananasi -- Breakers (?)<br /> Ananasi -- Kumo (organized, with kinfolk)<br /> Bastet -- Hishtpah (?)<br /> Bastet -- Hellcats (organized, I don't know about kinfolk)<br /> Camazotz -- Xibalan (individuals)<br /> Corax -- Carrion Crows/Buzzards (organized, but no kinfolk)<br /> Garou -- Black Spiral Dancers (organized, with kinfolk)<br /> Gurahl -- Purgers (individuals)<br /> Kitsune -- Kuko (individuals)<br /> Mokole -- Dumenkara/Mnetics (?)<br /> Nuwisha -- Bitter Grins (?)<br /> Ratkin -- Mad Destroyers (?)<br /> Ratkin -- Vermin (?)<br /> Rokea -- Balefire Sharks (?)<br /> Rokea -- Qyrl sharks (individuals)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-23-2015, 11:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:42:01-07:00","id":721760,"title":"","content":"Kumo devote themselves to the Wyrm as part of Queen Ananasa's master-plan/gambit.<br /> <br /> Antara are wildcards. The Queen relinquishes all control over them when they free themselves from her webs of manipulation and deceit. Being truly free to choose their own destiny some can choose to side with the Wyrm. Some go their own way independently of the Triat. This freedom from the Queen is why they are considered fallen. And why they are hated by other Ananasi even more than Ananasi hate the Kumo.<br /> <br /> Fallen Mokole have many many names. These are possibly the happiest of all Fallen breeds.<br /> <br /> Fallen Bastet are Histpah. I pity these more than most other fallen tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T01:32:20-07:00","id":722274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera?p=721595#post721595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you know of any way to access the Ozuzo article? I can't find it at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here you go. :-) <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-hidden-rain/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/the-hidden-rain/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T05:50:32-07:00","id":722733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera?p=721292#post721292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I listed references for all the ones I can remember -- in parentheses.<br /> Also I thought Skull Pigs were fomori, not actual genuine shapeshifters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found where it calls the fallen Kitsune Kuko in the lexicon but I wasn't able to find the Purgers in the Gurahl breed book.<br /> <br /> In the new wyrm book it says that the last of the Grondr Sounders who did not retreat to umbra gave into the Wyrm and became the first Skull Pigs. This makes the skull pigs the descendants of the fallen Grondr. At some point their corruption caused them to lose their ability to shape shift so they are what they are now. I would wager the same goes for the Xibalan and the Blood Bats. (botw20)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T07:22:36-07:00","id":722921,"title":"","content":"iv never heard of the bitter grins, are they just asshole nuwisha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T08:27:40-07:00","id":723129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nasrudin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera?p=722921#post722921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iv never heard of the bitter grins, are they just asshole nuwisha?</div> </div> </div> </div>But ....that's all nuwisha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:12:21-07:00","id":723476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nasrudin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera?p=722921#post722921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">iv never heard of the bitter grins, are they just asshole nuwisha?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much. Coyote and his pantheon of spirits (with the exception of Ptah) continue to serve the Bitter-Grin, though even Ptah does not inform other Nuwisha of his form charges fall. They continue to have access to all their normal gifts and gain access to wyrm gifts as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:20:47-07:00","id":723521,"title":"","content":"Thanks all!<br /> <br /> Derzhuzad, maybe Purgers were from MET also.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does anyone know what &quot;Breakers&quot; are?<br /> <br /> There are so many Ananasi groups. Damh\u00e0n serve the Queen. Atahsaia are weirdos in the Umbra and serve the Queen. Kumo serve the Wyrm but it's part of the Queen's plan. Kumatai serve themselves/the Wyld but it's probably part of the Queen's plan.<br /> <br /> Then there are Breakers and Padrone which I don't know what they are except their names, and there was some group in the Wyld West who served the Wyrm, I think, but I don't know their name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-24-2015, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T10:51:50-07:00","id":723622,"title":"","content":"Breakers are another name for Antara.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T16:06:28-07:00","id":724321,"title":"","content":"Shattered Dreams has a bit more info on the Grondr -&gt; Skullpigs connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T14:25:56-07:00","id":729882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera#post721171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are the different groups of fallen Fera and where are they detailed? I know of some but I want to ask if I am missing any?<br /> <br /> <br /> Ananasi -- Kumo (several books)<br /> Bastet -- Hishtpah (?) and Hellcats (Apocalypse)<br /> Camazotz -- Xibalan? (?)<br /> Corax -- Carrion Crows/Buzzards (?)<br /> Garou -- Black Spiral Dancers (lots of books)<br /> Gurahl -- Purgers (Gurahl breedbook)<br /> Kitsune -- Kuko (Hengeyokai)<br /> Mokole -- Dumenkara (?)<br /> Nuwisha -- Bitter Grins (?)<br /> Ratkin -- Vermin (?)<br /> Rokea -- Balefire Sharks (?) and anyone who makes a deal with Qyrl<br /> <br /> Ajaba -- ?<br /> Apis -- ?<br /> Grondr -- ?<br /> Nagah -- ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Please help.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what you're after is in BotW20. The Ozuzo have been linked here (I wrote them after a request from the forums here.)<br /> <br /> Some of the names you gave, and the ideas behind them possibly come from the Minds Eye Theatre book about fallen races. When writing several of these fallen races, I used that source for some of the titles and ideas, but ultimately they all came down to 'XX, but possessed by Banes!!' - I tried to instead go for something unique and thematic for each fallen breed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T15:52:33-07:00","id":730239,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it's probably an improvement then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Not that there isn't room for &quot;XX, but possessed by Banes!!&quot; as long as there's a thematic reason for it, like the zombie-fomori Gurahl that sometimes result when resurrection goes horribly wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T07:11:02-07:00","id":741701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/721171-fallen-fera?p=723521#post723521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks all!<br /> <br /> Derzhuzad, maybe Purgers were from MET also.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does anyone know what &quot;Breakers&quot; are?<br /> <br /> There are so many Ananasi groups. Damh\u00e0n serve the Queen. Atahsaia are weirdos in the Umbra and serve the Queen. Kumo serve the Wyrm but it's part of the Queen's plan. Kumatai serve themselves/the Wyld but it's probably part of the Queen's plan.<br /> <br /> Then there are Breakers and Padrone which I don't know what they are except their names, and there was some group in the Wyld West who served the Wyrm, I think, but I don't know their name.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Padrone are from the old Ananasi Breedbook. Essentially they are Ananasi who gain a new form which is described as kinda like the Pithus but horribly mutated with two vestigial legs to keep their prey at bay. Theyare cnanibalistic and attack Ananasi in their Sylie to kill and eat them. They appeared shortly after the War of Rage. Ananasa has not deigned herself to give her opinion of them to her children.<br /> <br /> Ananasa is kind of a piece of shit, to be honest.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-30T09:29:55-07:00","id":742077,"title":"","content":"Thanks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I must have read that at some point because I had written down when they appeared.<br /> <br /> And yeah, she kinda is.<br /> See also: what she made the Neanderthal Ananasi do to themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style